    "lawCode": "Amd §224-d, Lab L",
    "lawSection": "Labor Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8648\n\nSPONSOR: RAMOS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the labor law, in relation to redefining the term\n\"covered renewable energy system\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo redefine the term \"covered renewable energy system\" to include\nsystems with a capacity of one or more megawatts alternating current.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends subdivision 1 of section 224-d of the labor law, as\nadded by section 2 of part AA of chapter 56 of the laws of 2021.\nProvides the amended definition of a \"covered renewable energy\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nN/A\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe current definition of a \"covered renewable energy system\" only\nincludes systems with a capacity of greater than five megawatts alter-\nnating current. Amending the law to have the definition include systems\nwith one or more megawatts alternating current will encourage the\ncreation of construction jobs, many of which would be subject to\nprevailing wage. Increasing the number of distributed solar projects\nsubject to prevailing wage will benefit local workers, businesses, and\ncommunities.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE: :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
